<!--
  The OnlyFans mark is a light O with a darker F laid over it, and three things make it that mark
  rather than two letters. The O's counter is 0.29 of its outer radius, far tighter than any
  typeface draws one. The second letter sits *over* the O in the deeper of the two blues, so the
  overlap goes dark instead of knocking out. And that letter is slanted 20 degrees — its stem runs
  from upper right to lower left, which is what gives the mark its lean. All three are kept here,
  with an S in place of the F, because the name is the joke and the icon may as well be.

  So the O is geometry, not type: an evenOdd donut, radius 18 with a 5.22 counter, centred on
  43.58,54. The S is Archivo Black, which has no italic, so the 20 degrees is a shear about the
  baseline applied to the outline itself with fontTools — a VectorDrawable <group> can rotate,
  scale and translate but not skew, so it cannot be done at draw time. The path below is therefore
  not the plain glyph: re-extracting it from the .ttf means re-applying the shear.

  The shear costs size. It widens the glyph from 0.90 of its height to 1.05, and the lockup has to
  fit the same safe zone, so the O came down from radius 19.5 to 18. What sets the S's position is
  the counter: shearing forward swings the S's middle to the right and its lower bowl to the left,
  and it is the bowl that closes in on the hole. At 0.05 of the radius right of the O's centre the
  hole is still clean; at -0.05 it is not. Measured by rendering it, not by eye.

  The pair is centred on 54,54 and its furthest point is 30.8 out, inside the 33 the adaptive-icon
  safe zone allows. The colours are the logo's own two blues.
-->
